    "protectedRationale": "Caps exceed the largest per-arm run sd measured in the 2026-09-14/15 studies (agreement 0.107, whitespace 0.097, ECE 0.12 seen only in contaminated data; typical 0.02-0.07) so noise cannot veto; the rule still requires worsening beyond BOTH cap and pooled sd. Latency/token budgets reflect the known ~2x cost of the second pass - the trade-off is admitted up front, and exceeding it is a legitimate rejection ('complete trade-off better' or not).",
    "adoptionRule": "supported iff (signed improvement of target mean >= 0.08 AND bootstrap 90% CI lower bound of the signed improvement > 0 AND no protected metric regresses beyond its cap AND its pooled run sd AND usable runs >= 3/arm at reliability >= 0.75); inconclusive if usable runs < 2/arm; rejected otherwise. No threshold in config/judge-gates.json may change as part of adoption.",
